    {
      "id": "8vzntta",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Characteristics of Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Plant cells are characterized by a rigid cell wall composed of cellulose, plastids, and large central vacuoles.",
        "Plant tissues are broadly categorized into Meristematic tissues (actively dividing) and Permanent tissues (specialized).",
        "Photosynthesis utilizes solar energy, carbon dioxide, and water to produce glucose and release oxygen.",
        "Plant growth and physiological responses are regulated by key hormones including auxins, gibberellins, cytokinins, abscisic acid, and ethylene.",
        "Reproduction in plants occurs sexually through flowers and seeds, or asexually through vegetative propagation."
      ],
      "id": "y0ra1v9"
    },
